!!<*yamlover: $defs: chapter>
The storage axis
description: where a value lives, and what language it speaks
- |
  The storage concrete answers *where, in what language*: inline in an enclosing
  document, a whole file of its own, opaque bytes, or a directory. Two rules govern the
  axis. The **language-switch rule**: yamlover can switch to json5p mid-stream and yaml
  to json — never the reverse; after a switch, descendants take the switched language.
  And the **per-node rule**: every materialized node carries exactly one concrete,
  derived from the filesystem when unstated.
- *: inlined
- *: files
- *: binary
- *: directories
- *: multi-doc
